[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/django/django/issues/comments/244581123","html_url":"https://github.com/django/django/pull/7206#issuecomment-244581123","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/django/django/issues/7206","id":244581123,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI0NDU4MTEyMw==","user":{"login":"jarshwah","id":541083,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU0MTA4Mw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/541083?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jarshwah","html_url":"https://github.com/jarshwah","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jarshwah/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jarshwah/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jarshwah/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jarshwah/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jarshwah/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jarshwah/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jarshwah/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jarshwah/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jarshwah/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2016-09-04T02:45:45Z","updated_at":"2016-09-04T02:45:45Z","body":"I like the general idea here. Have you got a use case that this kind of instantiation will better support?\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/django/django/issues/comments/244581123/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/django/django/issues/comments/244581831","html_url":"https://github.com/django/django/pull/7206#issuecomment-244581831","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/django/django/issues/7206","id":244581831,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI0NDU4MTgzMQ==","user":{"login":"cjerdonek","id":355822,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1NTgyMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/355822?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cjerdonek","html_url":"https://github.com/cjerdonek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cjerdonek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cjerdonek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cjerdonek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cjerdonek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cjerdonek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cjerdonek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cjerdonek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cjerdonek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cjerdonek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2016-09-04T03:13:13Z","updated_at":"2016-09-04T03:13:13Z","body":"Well, pretty much anytime you might want to customize or otherwise change the behavior of a database backend that involves changing one of the six classes instantiated inside the `__init__()` method (including `DatabaseClient`, `DatabaseCreation`, etc).\n\nFor example, if [this ticket](https://code.djangoproject.com/ticket/27061) hadn't been accepted, I would have been able to subclass the PostgreSQL backend, where the only difference in the class definition would be setting the `creation_class` class attribute to a subclass of the PostgreSQL `DatabaseCreation` class. Without this patch, subclassing the backend would be messier and more likely to require copy-and-pasting code from Django's code base.\n\nI also think this implementation is better from a design and maintenance perspective. For example, the code is now more DRY. (Observe that the patch actually has a net reduction in the number of lines, though the number of lines isn't actually the important part.)\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/django/django/issues/comments/244581831/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/django/django/issues/comments/244581946","html_url":"https://github.com/django/django/pull/7206#issuecomment-244581946","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/django/django/issues/7206","id":244581946,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI0NDU4MTk0Ng==","user":{"login":"cjerdonek","id":355822,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1NTgyMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/355822?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cjerdonek","html_url":"https://github.com/cjerdonek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cjerdonek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cjerdonek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cjerdonek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cjerdonek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cjerdonek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cjerdonek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cjerdonek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cjerdonek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cjerdonek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2016-09-04T03:17:11Z","updated_at":"2016-09-04T03:17:59Z","body":"You can also see the effect of this patch \"in action\" by looking at how the `gis` backend (which is a customization of the mysql backend) is now defined. The only differences from the `MySQLDatabaseWrapper` are the values of a few of the class attributes.\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/django/django/issues/comments/244581946/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/django/django/issues/comments/244582074","html_url":"https://github.com/django/django/pull/7206#issuecomment-244582074","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/django/django/issues/7206","id":244582074,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI0NDU4MjA3NA==","user":{"login":"jarshwah","id":541083,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU0MTA4Mw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/541083?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jarshwah","html_url":"https://github.com/jarshwah","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jarshwah/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jarshwah/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jarshwah/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jarshwah/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jarshwah/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jarshwah/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jarshwah/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jarshwah/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jarshwah/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2016-09-04T03:21:31Z","updated_at":"2016-09-04T03:21:31Z","body":"Sorry, my original message wasn't clear at all (had just woken up). \n\nI was interested in hearing about specific uses you had planned with this change. It's not often we see backends being customised, so I wanted to know a little more about the customisations you were looking into. It's not often people make refactorings like this just for purity sake - there's usually a goal. The creation_class for testing is a good example though, thanks.\n\nI totally agree this patch makes things look a lot nicer and simpler too. 👍 \n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/django/django/issues/comments/244582074/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/django/django/issues/comments/244582233","html_url":"https://github.com/django/django/pull/7206#issuecomment-244582233","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/django/django/issues/7206","id":244582233,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI0NDU4MjIzMw==","user":{"login":"cjerdonek","id":355822,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1NTgyMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/355822?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cjerdonek","html_url":"https://github.com/cjerdonek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cjerdonek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cjerdonek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cjerdonek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cjerdonek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cjerdonek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cjerdonek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cjerdonek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cjerdonek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cjerdonek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2016-09-04T03:28:04Z","updated_at":"2016-09-04T03:28:04Z","body":"Oh, okay, thanks. :) As far as concrete things for the future, I didn't have anything specific in mind at the moment. But the type of thing I could see it being useful for in the near-term is if, say, I wanted to add or tweak any of the logging being done by at some point by a backend. That kind of thing would be probably be special or temporary enough where it wouldn't be worth (or not be appropriate for) upstreaming to Django. \n\nAnother possibility is [this ticket](https://code.djangoproject.com/ticket/27074), which had a possibility of not being (and still might not be) accepted.\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/django/django/issues/comments/244582233/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/django/django/issues/comments/244582324","html_url":"https://github.com/django/django/pull/7206#issuecomment-244582324","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/django/django/issues/7206","id":244582324,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI0NDU4MjMyNA==","user":{"login":"cjerdonek","id":355822,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1NTgyMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/355822?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cjerdonek","html_url":"https://github.com/cjerdonek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cjerdonek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cjerdonek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cjerdonek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cjerdonek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cjerdonek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cjerdonek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cjerdonek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cjerdonek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cjerdonek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2016-09-04T03:31:17Z","updated_at":"2016-09-04T03:31:17Z","body":"Here's [one more example](https://code.djangoproject.com/ticket/26282) of backend behavior that could be facilitated by this patch. This one _was_ closed as \"won't fix.\"\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/django/django/issues/comments/244582324/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/django/django/issues/comments/245005207","html_url":"https://github.com/django/django/pull/7206#issuecomment-245005207","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/django/django/issues/7206","id":245005207,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI0NTAwNTIwNw==","user":{"login":"timgraham","id":411869,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxMTg2OQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/411869?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/timgraham","html_url":"https://github.com/timgraham","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timgraham/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timgraham/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timgraham/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timgraham/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timgraham/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timgraham/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timgraham/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timgraham/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timgraham/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2016-09-06T16:19:15Z","updated_at":"2016-09-06T16:19:15Z","body":"Don't forget about the contrib.gis database backends.\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/django/django/issues/comments/245005207/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/django/django/issues/comments/245022695","html_url":"https://github.com/django/django/pull/7206#issuecomment-245022695","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/django/django/issues/7206","id":245022695,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI0NTAyMjY5NQ==","user":{"login":"cjerdonek","id":355822,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1NTgyMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/355822?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cjerdonek","html_url":"https://github.com/cjerdonek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cjerdonek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cjerdonek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cjerdonek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cjerdonek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cjerdonek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cjerdonek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cjerdonek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cjerdonek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cjerdonek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2016-09-06T17:18:12Z","updated_at":"2016-09-06T17:18:12Z","body":"> Don't forget about the contrib.gis database backends.\n\nThose classes are already changed by the patch. Do you mean in the tests? I'm almost positive the contrib.gis backends are already being tested by this patch to the extent that they're reflected in the test matrix / configuration. For example, in the \"spatialite\" test run, the \"`conn`\" in the test will be an instance of the `DatabaseWrapper` class defined in `spatialite/base.py`.\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/django/django/issues/comments/245022695/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/django/django/issues/comments/245307027","html_url":"https://github.com/django/django/pull/7206#issuecomment-245307027","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/django/django/issues/7206","id":245307027,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI0NTMwNzAyNw==","user":{"login":"timgraham","id":411869,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxMTg2OQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/411869?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/timgraham","html_url":"https://github.com/timgraham","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timgraham/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timgraham/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timgraham/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timgraham/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timgraham/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timgraham/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timgraham/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timgraham/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timgraham/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2016-09-07T14:55:13Z","updated_at":"2016-09-07T14:55:13Z","body":"Now I wonder if my advice about describing the problem in the commit message is backfiring. \"Made database backends easier to subclass.\" is a bit nebulous about how subclassing is eased. Perhaps something like \"Eased subclassing DatabaseWrapper by adding class attributes for helper classes.\" might be better.\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/django/django/issues/comments/245307027/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]